@node CMacs AI Menu
@chapter CMacs AI Menu: the Universal Right-Click

@cindex AI menu
@cindex context menu
@cindex right-click

Right-click anywhere in cmacs and the AI is there, acting on whatever
you clicked.  A region, a file in dired, a failing test in a compilation
buffer, a diff hunk, an org heading, the last command in a terminal, a
note in the roamgraph -- each is understood as itself, not flattened to
``the buffer''.

The feature is four layers, and the split is the point: adding a new
place the menu works means writing one @dfn{resolver}, and adding a new
thing the menu can do means writing one @dfn{action}.  Neither has to
know the other exists, and nothing anywhere grows a @code{cond} over
major modes.

@multitable @columnfractions .22 .38 .40
@headitem Layer @tab File @tab Answers
@item Menu backends @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-menu.el}
  @tab how do I draw a menu here?
@item Targets @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-target.el}
  @tab what is under the click?
@item Resolvers @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-targets.el}
  @tab @dots{} in @emph{this} kind of buffer
@item Actions @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-actions.el}
  @tab what can be done with it?
@item Text operations @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-textops.el}
  @tab summarize / rephrase / reply
@item Result window @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-output.el}
  @tab where the answer goes
@item Wiring @tab @file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-menu.el}
  @tab the context-menu entry and bootstrap
@end multitable

Requires @option{--with-cmacs-ai}.  The Brigade group additionally
requires @option{--with-cmacs-ai-brigade}, and the Chat group's
libreclaw entry @option{--with-cmacs-libreclaw}; each group simply does
not appear when its subsystem is not in the build.

